<h2>A different buyer, not just a longer shipping lane</h2>
<p>It's tempting to think of the US basmati market as simply "the Gulf trade with a longer transit," but the buyer profile is genuinely different. US demand runs through ethnic-grocery retail and foodservice distribution serving South Asian and broader diaspora communities, plus growing general-market interest in basmati as a premium long-grain rice — not the national-staple-scale bulk consumption that drives Iraqi or Saudi demand. At roughly USD 341 million in 2024-25, it's still a leading market, but the order profile — smaller, more varied, more retail-format-sensitive — reflects that different structure.</p>

<h2>FSVP means more paperwork exchange than most markets</h2>
<p>More than any other basmati market we serve, the US channels import compliance through a specific documented system: FSVP puts verification responsibility on your importer, but they can only satisfy it with information and documentation from us — product specifications, processing detail, supporting records. First-time US buyers should expect a longer, more document-heavy onboarding than a Gulf order, even though the actual shipping and grading process is the same.</p>

<h2>25-35 days means planning around demand peaks, not just lead time</h2>
<p>At more than double the transit time of most Gulf lanes, US basmati orders need genuine inventory planning — particularly around demand peaks tied to South Asian festival and holiday calendars, where a late-ordered shipment simply won't arrive in time. Build your reorder point around the full 25-35 day window rather than the shorter lead times that work fine on our faster lanes.</p>

<h2>Packaging format follows the channel</h2>
<p>Because US demand splits across retail, foodservice and food-manufacturing buyers rather than concentrating in one channel, packaging format varies more here than in staple markets. Retail-bound orders commonly run smaller bags (1-10kg, often private-label), while foodservice and manufacturing buyers take standard bulk bag formats. Tell us which channel you're supplying and we'll match the packaging rather than defaulting to one format.</p>

